  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "OT::NameRecord::copy",
    "file": "harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-name-table.hh",
    "description": "Heap OOB read is caused by copying name-string bytes using untrusted NameRecord fields without validating bounds against the source name table storage area. In NameRecord::copy(), `out->offset.serialize_copy(c, src_base + offset, dst_base, length)` uses attacker-controlled `offset` and `length` directly. This builds an `hb_array_t` over `src_base+offset` with `length` bytes, and `hb_array_t::copy` then reads `arrayZ[i]` up to `length`, causing read past allocation when offset/length point outside the actual string pool.",
    "conditions": "Triggered in hb-subset-fuzzer during name table subsetting (`OT::name::subset` -> `name::serialize` -> `NameRecord::copy`). A crafted font with malformed `name` table record(s) where `NameRecord.offset` and/or `NameRecord.length` are inconsistent with actual string storage causes `serialize_copy` to copy from an invalid source pointer. The PoC provides such a malformed name table, leading to ASan heap-buffer-overflow read in `hb_array_t::copy`."
  },
